Same algorithm: count the bytes, build the tree, build the codes, pack the bits one at a time (the reference's inner loop over a code's bits). The tree's Box nodes are arrays (9 nodes) and the list is an array moved with array.move where the reference uses Vec::remove/insert. Other stores are range-checked; state is unlogged, so nothing is saved for a rollback. Scratch state rebuilt every run (the reference's locals: out) is not logged (state is unlogged by default, so no undo log, as a Rust local has none).
